Calculus and differential-equation preparation — Strang and Herman, OpenStax (@ic-calculus: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_027WKVM5NG5X84M86TSVRA77J3
Gilbert Strang and Edwin “Jed” Herman. Calculus, Volumes 1 and 2, OpenStax, originally published 30 March 2016, with later revisions. [Volume 1](https://openstax.org/books/calculus-volume-1/pages/1-introduction) · [Volume 2](https://openstax.org/books/calculus-volume-2/pages/1-introduction) · [Differential equations, Volume 2 chapter 4](https://openstax.org/books/calculus-volume-2/pages/4-introduction).

Use the complete relevant limits, differentiation, integration and application chapters of Volume 1, then the entire differential-equation chapter of Volume 2 for changing-inventory models. Work the examples and exercises independently; read whole volumes for a fuller mathematical foundation where needed. The chemical-model Record supplies the connecting meanings rather than duplicating an entire calculus course.

Author/date, chapter structure and current notices were checked on 29 October 2026. The current web/PDF notices identify CC BY-NC-SA 4.0; some older PDFs retain CC BY 4.0. Preserve the actual version and its attribution/component terms rather than silently treating every edition as having identical rights. The book pages, figures and assessment material remain external links.

**Return:** [Industrial chemistry sources — whole books, courses, technical methods and primary evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3084780FHMK499ZDAW07TYA3TQ).
